{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_015rgTeEBHqhxTpZ71eGc7j4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good question — and it's by design, not a bug:\n\n**The samples and the comparison reel are intentionally silent.** They're picture-only direction samples, so I stripped audio (`-an`) when building them — and the Kling clips themselves were generated with audio off (cheaper, and we don't want Kling's invented audio). The reel is just for choosing the *visual* direction.\n\n**The actual film has sound.** The assembled cut — `review-room/review-room-v1.mp4` — already carries the video-claw `$0` TTS narration + the silent-anchored/loudnorm'd audio track (ffprobe shows an `aac` stream). So the real deliverable isn't silent; only these throwaway samples are.\n\nTwo things I can do if it helps:\n- **Lay the narration (or a scratch music bed) under the comparison reel** so you can judge the samples with sound — quick to add, just say the word.\n- If you watched **`review-room-v1.mp4`** and *that* played silent for you, that'd be a player/track issue worth a look — tell me and I'll check it (but the audio stream is in there).\n\nFor picking directions, silent is usually fine — you're choosing look/motion, and the same VO drops over whatever we pick. Want me to add audio to the reel anyway, or are you good to call the directions from the visuals?"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":629006,"cache_read_input_tokens":16914,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":629006},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":{"cache_miss_reason":{"type":"previous_message_not_found"}},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8372a238-b04e-409c-9415-57d1f26ec648","uuid":"4cb0a4f2-9609-43e5-97ad-bcbf40da7f05","request_id":"req_011CbcukxBF8Dd978